BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 397.77 Tm (The first trap is the buyer's own head. Emmanuel Ak says most beginners lose money because they are too) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 382.55 Tm (emotional, so he builds his selection process on numbers instead of taste [RsyNgibgVJY @ 00:00:38].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 367.32 Tm (Ticket Flipping shows where that emotion costs cash on the seat map. Buyers chasing the front rows paid) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 352.10 Tm ($234, while seats one row back cost about $125. Those seats can be listed at $200 for a profit while still) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 336.87 Tm (undercutting the front row [GORTWFnPPt0 @ 00:01:41]. The same channel says that 99% of the time you) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 321.65 Tm (do not want platinum tickets because they are overpriced. It also flags dynamic pricing as a trap: a $50) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 306.42 Tm (primary ticket gets relabeled as an $80 platinum seat once resale sits at $80 [hw92haJDs9Y @ 00:12:52].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 291.20 Tm (The fix Emmanuel Ak teaches is a live comparison before checkout. Keep the tickets in your cart and check) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 275.97 Tm (the resale market first, because people list early or hold insider tickets. He did this on Rush seats that cost) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 260.75 Tm (about $300 and were listed near $570, about $270 profit per ticket [RsyNgibgVJY @ 00:25:17]. Skip that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 245.52 Tm (check, and an operator ends up buying at or above what the secondary market will actually pay, with no) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 230.30 Tm (margin left to cover fees or a slow sale.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 215.07 Tm (The second trap is fake scarcity. Ticket Flipping lists four warnings from their inventory-tracking method) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 199.85 Tm ([hw92haJDs9Y @ 00:11:21]:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 184.62 Tm (- Held inventory released back into a show can push the count from 500 up to 700. They want two or three) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 169.40 Tm (large drops relative to capacity before trusting a trend.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 154.17 Tm (- Duds show few tickets left but no movement.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 138.95 Tm (- Dynamic pricing hides the real get-in.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 123.72 Tm (- Some shows simply lack demand, with primary at $50 while secondary sits at $45.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 108.50 Tm (They add that there can always be one or two people selling for a loss. Judge the majority of listings across) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 93.27 Tm (StubHub, Vivid Seats and TickPick, not the first few [hw92haJDs9Y @ 00:13:38]. Emmanuel Ak warns that) Tj ET
